// Title: Invoke-Obfuscation Via Use MSHTA
// Sigma ID: ac20ae82-8758-4f38-958e-b44a3140ca88
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nikita Nazarov, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-08 | Modified: 2022-03-08
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027, execution, T1059.001
// Description: Detects Obfuscated Powershell via use MSHTA in Scripts
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/issues/1009
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_invoke_obfuscation_via_use_mhsta.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "set" and ProcessCommandLine contains "&&" and ProcessCommandLine contains "mshta" and ProcessCommandLine contains "vbscript:createobject" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".run" and ProcessCommandLine contains "(window.close)"
